Limitations

1. You may use or modify the software for your own internal business purposes,
   including operating storefronts for your company, or for non-commercial,
   research, educational, or personal use. Your company may sell its own or
   resold goods, services, and digital products to customers through these
   storefronts. Customer-facing product pages, accounts, agent interactions,
   APIs, and checkout are permitted as part of that own-business use.

2. Without a separate written commercial license from the applicable rights
   holders, you must not use the software or derivative works to offer third
   parties a commercial ecommerce platform, shop builder, commerce backend,
   managed shop-hosting service, or software-as-a-service. This includes
   providing independent merchants with shops, administration, commerce APIs,
   or agent-accessible commerce services operated on their behalf; reselling,
   white-labeling, or commercially embedding the software in such an offering;
   and selling or licensing copies of the software or derivative works as a
   competing shop system. The restriction applies whether charges are direct,
   bundled with other services, or indirect, and whether the software is
   modified, rebranded, single-tenant, or multi-tenant.

3. You may distribute copies or modifications free of charge, provided that
   recipients receive this license and their use remains subject to it. You
   may charge for consulting, development, installation, or maintenance of a
   customer's own-business installation, provided that this is not a sale or
   license of the software and does not provide the prohibited hosted or
   managed commerce offering described above. Purchasing ordinary computing
   infrastructure to operate your own storefronts is permitted.

4. You may not alter, remove, or obscure licensing, copyright, or other notices
   of the licensor. Use of the licensor's trademarks is subject to applicable
